-- title:
--   Consistency To Almost Projective Right
-- statement:
--   **Consistency makes Bob's right-lifted measurement almost projective.**
--
--   Let $H_A$ and $H_B$ be finite local index sets, let $\psi$ be a quantum state on $H_A\otimes H_B$, and let $A$ and $B$ be finite-outcome measurements on the two registers. No normalization assumption on $\psi$ is required. If the constant families of $A$ and $B$ are $\zeta$-consistent under the uniform singleton question distribution, then the right-lifted measurement $\widehat B$ with effects $\widehat B_a=I_{H_A}\otimes B_a$ satisfies the almost-projective conditions with parameter $2\zeta$:
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   &\operatorname{SSCRel}(\psi,\widehat B)\le 2\zeta,\\
--   &\operatorname{SDDRel}(\psi,\widehat B,\widehat B)\le 4\zeta,\\
--   &\sum_a\operatorname{ev}_{\psi}\!\left(\widehat B_a-\widehat B_a^2\right)\le 2\zeta.
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   The middle bound is $4\zeta$ because the almost-projective predicate records self-distance with twice its parameter. This is the right-register input to `orthonormalizationMeasurement_right_of_consistency_from_projectivizationRepair_heterogeneous`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.consistencyToAlmostProjective_right`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective/Projectivization.lean#L485-L535

